# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=DAC
Version=dacif_v2_0_U3_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
DAC_Channel|Channel|||||
DAC_HighFrequency|DAC High Frequency Mode|Common DAC Settings||||High frequency mode is disabled in LPBAM context
DAC_AutonomousMode|Autonomous mode|Common DAC Settings||||Autonomous mode is mandatory in LPBAM context
DAC_DMADoubleDataMode|DMA double data mode|||||Specifies if DMA double data mode should be enabled or not
DAC_SignedFormat|Signed Format|||||Specifies if signed format should be used or not
DAC_Trigger|Trigger|||||Specifies the external trigger for the selected DAC channel. A selection of a Trigger allows the activation of a Triangle or Noise Wave generation mode
DAC_OutputBuffer_OUT1|Output Buffer|||||The activation/deactivation of the buffer is linked to the combination the mode selected and the out connection. Buffer could be enabled only if "OUT mode" is at least connected to the external pin (with or without the on chip peripheral connection) Buffer could be disabled is not possible in two case : - "OUT mode" connected to external pin only with Sample and Hold selected mode - "OUT mode" connected to external pin and internal on chip peripheral with the Normal selected mode
DAC_OutputBuffer_OUT2|Output Buffer|||||The activation/deactivation of the buffer is linked to the combination the mode selected and the out connection. Buffer could be enabled only if "OUT mode" is at least connected to the external pin (with or without the on chip peripheral connection) Buffer could be disabled is not possible in two case : - "OUT mode" connected to external pin only with Sample and Hold selected mode - "OUT mode" connected to external pin and internal on chip peripheral with the Normal selected mode
WaveGeneration|Wave generation mode|||||Selection of the wave generation : Triangle or Noise
TriangleAmplitude|Maximum Triangle Amplitude|||||This small-amplitude triangular waveform is adde to the output. The triangle counter is incremented three as long as it is less than the maximum amplitude Once the configured amplitude is reached, the counter is decremented down to 0, then incremented again and so on.
NoiseAmplitude|Noise Amplitude|||||In order to generate a variable-amplitude pseudonoise, an LFSR (linear feedback shift register) is available.
DAC1_ConnectOnChipPeripheral|Connect On Chip Peripheral1|||||
DAC2_ConnectOnChipPeripheral|Connect On Chip Peripheral2|||||Specifies whether the DAC output is connected or not to on chip peripheral .
DAC_UserTrimming|User Trimming|||||Specifies the trimming mode This parameter must be a value of DAC User Trimming DAC_UserTrimming is either factory or user trimming
DAC_TrimmingValue|Trimming Value|||1|31|Specifies the offset trimming value.
DAC_SampleAndHold|Mode selected|||||Specifies the DAC mode which is Smple and Hold in LPBA context
DAC_SampleTime|Sample Time|||0|1023|On Sample and Hold Mode : Specifies the Sample time
DAC_HoldTime|Hold Time|||0|1023|On Sample and Hold Mode : Specifies the hold time
DAC_RefreshTime|Refresh Time|||0|255|On Sample and Hold Mode : Specifies the refresh time
Interrupt1|DMA underrun error for DAC1_CH1|IP Internal Interrupt||||description
Interrupt2|DMA underrun error for DAC1_CH2|IP Internal Interrupt||||description
ORingInterrupt|Interrupt parameter for code generation __HAL_DAC_ENABLE_IT|||||

